issues:
Major: Import argument expansion discards the quote metadata required by the new block-delimiter checks. caddyconfig/caddyfile/parse.go:367. Example: `(reply) {
 respond {args[0]} 200
}
:8080 {
 import reply "{"
}` still fails with "Unexpected next token after '{' on same line": RemainingArgs converts the quoted argument to a string, and doImport substitutes it into the unquoted placeholder token, turning the literal brace into a block opener. Variadic argument expansion has the same problem. Fix: retain argument tokens and propagate their quoted status when substituting arguments, including variadic expansion; add regression tests for imported quoted opening and closing braces.
